<title>CANADA: Job stability key to consumer health - study.</title>
<headline>Job stability key to consumer health - study.</headline>
<dateline>TORONTO 1996-11-08</dateline>
<text>
<p>Canadian consumers are keeping a tight grip on their wallets because of a lack of stable, full-time, well-paid jobs, according to a study released on Friday by a major Canadian bank.</p>
<p>The increase in overall employment during the past three years -- a time of supposed economic recovery -- was accompanied by a steady decline in the quality of employment, the study by the Canadian Imperial Bank of Commerce (CIBC) showed.</p>
</text>
